				The aging system feels far too aggressive. Once a boxer reaches the age of 26–27, their stats suddenly start declining at an unrealistic rate.

At 26–27, a professional boxer is still in their prime. There's no reason for an athlete to experience such a significant drop in performance simply because of aging. At that age, major stat reductions should only occur as a consequence of serious injuries or substantial damage sustained during fights.

I would suggest introducing a gradual decline in physical ...			&lt;/div&gt;
